#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""One-file builder for FRED_Credit_Risk_Dashboard.

Plain ASCII (the code rides inside as base64), so it survives corporate
email and DLP intact. Run it on the target machine and it BUILDS the
workbook locally -- nothing binary is ever transmitted.

USAGE (PowerShell):
    python -m pip install pandas openpyxl
    python build_dashboard.py

It writes into the current folder:
    FRED_Credit_Risk_Dashboard.xlsm           (macro embedded, demo-populated)
    FRED_Credit_Risk_Dashboard_fallback.xlsx  (no VBA; if Excel rejects the .xlsm, open this,
                      paste macro.bas via Alt+F11, save as .xlsm)
    runner.py, macro.bas, requirements.txt

Refresh later, with the workbook CLOSED:
    python runner.py --workbook ".\\FRED_Credit_Risk_Dashboard.xlsm" --demo
    python runner.py --workbook ".\\FRED_Credit_Risk_Dashboard.xlsm"   # LIVE -- needs FRED_API_KEY
    Live FRED pulls need a free API key in the FRED_API_KEY environment
    variable (or the fred_api_key cell in _config).
"""
